## Pack the Compute Image

The compute image is now complete. Pack it and associate it with the *compute*
group so the nodes have something to boot. `--nosyncfiles` keeps the synclist's
files out of the packed image; the nodes receive them at boot. The image build
also leaves a munge key of its own in the chroot (the Slurm packages create one
when none exists). Remove it, so that munge on the nodes starts only with the
head's key. A site that sets a root password in the xCAT `passwd` table should
also set `chdef -t site secureroot=1`, so that `packimage` does not write that
password hash into the image.

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Pack compute image and associate it with the compute group -->
```bash
# The nodes get the munge key from the head at boot, not from the image
rm -f ${CHROOT}/etc/munge/munge.key
packimage --nosyncfiles ${xcat_osimage}

# Associate provisioning image for compute group
nodeset compute osimage=${xcat_osimage}
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->
